{
  "isoCode": "NO",
  "title": "Ja, vi elsker dette landet",
  "language": {
    "code": "no",
    "name": "Norwegian",
    "script": "Latin"
  },
  "sources": {
    "local": {
      "author": "Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson",
      "licence": "Public domain",
      "note": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ja,_vi_elsker_dette_landet"
    },
    "english": {
      "author": "English Wikipedia contributors",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "note": "Extracted from the English Wikipedia article cited in sources.local.note."
    }
  },
  "verses": [
    {
      "local": [
        "Ja, vi elsker dette landet,",
        "som det stiger frem,",
        "furet, værbitt over vannet,",
        "med de tusen hjem, —"
      ],
      "english": [
        "Yes, we love this land,",
        "as it rises,",
        "furrowed, weather-beaten over the water,",
        "with its thousand homes, —"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "elsker, elsker det og tenker",
        "på vår far og mor",
        "og den saganatt som",
        "drømmer på vår jord."
      ],
      "english": [
        "love, love it and think",
        "of our father and mother",
        "and the legendary night that lowers",
        "dreams upon our earth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Dette landet Harald berget",
        "med sin kjemperad,",
        "dette landet Håkon verget,",
        "medens Øyvind kvad;"
      ],
      "english": [
        "This country Harald united",
        "with his army of heroes,",
        "this country Håkon protected",
        "whilst Øyvind sung;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Olav på det landet malet",
        "korset med sitt blod,",
        "fra dets høye Sverre",
        "Roma midt imot."
      ],
      "english": [
        "upon the country Olav painted",
        "with his blood the cross,",
        "from its heights Sverre spoke",
        "up against Rome."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Bønder sine økser brynte",
        "hvor en hær dro frem;",
        "Tordenskjold langs kysten lynte,",
        "så den lystes hjem."
      ],
      "english": [
        "Farmers their axes sharpened",
        "wherever an army advanced,",
        "Tordenskjold along the coastline thundered",
        "so that we could see it back home."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Kvinner selv stod opp og strede",
        "som de vare menn;",
        "andre kunne bare grede,",
        "men igjen!"
      ],
      "english": [
        "Even women stood up and fought",
        "as if they were men;",
        "others could only cry",
        "but that soon would end!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Visstnok var vi ikke mange,",
        "men vi strakk dog til,",
        "da vi prøvdes noen gange,",
        "og det stod på spill;"
      ],
      "english": [
        "Sure, we were not many",
        "but we were enough,",
        "when we were tested sometimes,",
        "and it was at stake;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "ti vi heller landet brente",
        "enn det kom til fall;",
        "husker bare hva som",
        "ned på Fredrikshald!"
      ],
      "english": [
        "we would rather burn our land",
        "than to declare defeat;",
        "just remember what happened",
        "down at Fredrikshald!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Hårde tider har vi døyet,",
        "ble til sist forstøtt;",
        "men i verste nød blåøyet",
        "frihet ble oss født."
      ],
      "english": [
        "Hard times we have coped with,",
        "were at last disowned;",
        "but in the worst distress, blue-eyed",
        "freedom was to us born."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Det gav faderkraft å bære",
        "hungersnød og krig,",
        "det gav døden selv sin ære —",
        "og forlik."
      ],
      "english": [
        "It gave us father's strength to carry",
        "famine and war,",
        "it gave death itself its honour –",
        "and it gave reconciliation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Fienden sitt våpen kastet,",
        "opp visiret fór,",
        "vi med undren mot ham hastet,",
        "ti han var vår bror."
      ],
      "english": [
        "The enemy threw away his weapon,",
        "up the visor went,",
        "we, in wonder, to him hastened,",
        "because he was our brother."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Drevne frem på stand av skammen,",
        "gikk vi søderpå;",
        "nå står vi tre brødre sammen,",
        "og skal stå!"
      ],
      "english": [
        "Driven forth to a stand by shame",
        "we went to the south;",
        "now we three brothers stand united,",
        "and shall stand like that!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "[[Norske]] mann i hus og hytte,",
        "takk din store Gud!",
        "Landet ville han beskytte,",
        "skjønt det mørkt så ut."
      ],
      "english": [
        "[[Norwegian]] man in house and cabin,",
        "thank your great God!",
        "The country he wanted to protect,",
        "although things looked dark."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Alt, hva fedrene har kjempet,",
        "mødrene har grett,",
        "har den Herre stille lempet,",
        "så vår rett."
      ],
      "english": [
        "All that the fathers have fought [for],",
        "and the mothers have wept [over],",
        "the Lord has quietly eased",
        "so we won our rights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Ja, vi elsker dette landet,",
        "som det stiger frem,",
        "furet, værbitt over vannet,",
        "med de tusen hjem."
      ],
      "english": [
        "Yes, we love this country",
        "as it rises forth,",
        "rugged, weathered, above the sea,",
        "with those thousand homes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "local": [
        "Og som fedres kamp har hevet",
        "det av nød til seir,",
        "også vi, når det blir krevet,",
        "for slår leir."
      ],
      "english": [
        "And as the fathers' struggle has raised",
        "it from need to victory,",
        "even we, when it is demanded,",
        "for its peace will encamp."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
